<description>
Fill the frame interior with two marker colors arranged in matching 2x2 diagonal quadrants.

Input structure:
- The dominant background contains one solid one-pixel-thick rectangular frame.
- The frame has an even-height and even-width empty interior.
- Exactly two one-pixel markers of different colors sit outside the frame.

Rule:
- A marker in the northwest or southeast side of the frame center supplies the
  main diagonal quadrants of the interior.
- A marker in the northeast or southwest side supplies the other two quadrants.
- Split the frame interior into row and column halves and fill each cell by
  the diagonal class of its half-position.

Key insight:
- The marker colors are not copied from their exact rows or columns; their
  coarse position relative to the frame center selects one of the two diagonal
  quadrant masks.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "two singleton color marker pixels s outside the frame",
  "dst": "opposite-quadrant masks d formed by splitting the frame interior into row and column halves",
  "match_cond": "NW/SE markers match the TL+BR mask; NE/SW markers match the TR+BL mask",
  "transform": "fill each matched interior mask with s.color; preserve the frame and markers"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 8-14 rows x 8-14 cols (all eval: 10x10) [observed]
  background: single color filling most cells
  frame:
    shape: 1-pixel-thick solid rectangular border, single non-bg color
    interior: even height x even width, 2-8 cells per dimension; filled with bg
    placement: >=1 cell margin from grid edges on all sides
  markers:
    count: exactly 2 singleton pixels outside the frame
    colors: distinct from each other, from bg, and from frame color
    positions: each at a corner diagonal of the frame (r0-1,c0-1), (r0-1,c1+1), (r1+1,c0-1), or (r1+1,c1+1)
    diagonal_constraint: one on main diagonal (NW or SE corner) and one on anti diagonal (NE or SW corner)
  output:
    frame interior split into 4 equal quadrants (top-left, top-right, bottom-left, bottom-right)
    main-diagonal quadrants (TL + BR) filled with the main-diagonal marker color
    anti-diagonal quadrants (TR + BL) filled with the anti-diagonal marker color
    frame, markers, and background unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size H x W (8-14, even recommended for symmetry).
    2. Pick frame outer dimensions Fh x Fw where Fh, Fw >= 4 and interior (Fh-2) x (Fw-2) is even in both dims.
    3. Place frame with >=1 cell margin from all grid edges. Choose frame color != bg.
    4. Pick 2 distinct marker colors != bg, != frame color.
    5. Choose one main-diagonal corner (NW or SE) and one anti-diagonal corner (NE or SW) of the frame.
    6. Place markers at the selected corner-diagonal positions.
    7. Fill interior quadrants: TL+BR with main-diagonal marker color, TR+BL with anti-diagonal marker color. This is the output.
    8. To get input, clear the interior to background color.
```
